WEBVTT

1
00:00:27.105 --> 00:00:31.565
<i>Now the latest weather forecast
for northwest Koriko.</i>

2
00:00:31.676 --> 00:00:34.804
<i>Skies are clearing up,
thanks to a high-pressure front...</i>

3
00:00:34.912 --> 00:00:37.938
<i>moving in from the continent.</i>

4
00:00:38.049 --> 00:00:41.416
<i>Mild winds will be
blowing in from the west...</i>

5
00:00:41.519 --> 00:00:44.420
<i>clearing out the clouds
by this evening.</i>

6
00:00:44.522 --> 00:00:47.457
<i>We'll also have
a beautiful full moon tonight...</i>

7
00:00:47.558 --> 00:00:51.460
<i>so pack up your picnic baskets because
the weather is going to be just fine.</i>

8
00:00:53.297 --> 00:00:56.357
<i>More news in just a minute.</i>

9
00:00:57.235 --> 00:01:00.136
<i>First this word from
the courteous people at Central Market.</i>

10
00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:31.898
Jiji, I've decided!
I'm gonna do it tonight!

11
00:01:32.870 --> 00:01:35.668
Mom! Hey! I decided!

12
00:01:35.773 --> 00:01:38.833
Oh, hi, Miss Dora.
It's gonna be completely clear tonight.

13
00:01:38.943 --> 00:01:42.606
I heard the weather forecast.
There's gonna be a big full moon.

14
00:01:42.713 --> 00:01:45.841
Did you borrow your father's radio
without permission again?

15
00:01:45.950 --> 00:01:47.679
Is it okay? I'm sorry!

16
00:01:48.453 --> 00:01:50.353
Happy to see you, Miss Dora.

17
00:01:50.455 --> 00:01:52.423
Mom, my mind's made up.
It's tonight.

18
00:01:52.523 --> 00:01:55.253
Weren't you gonna
put it off a month?

19
00:01:55.359 --> 00:01:57.850
But the next full moon
might be on a cloudy night.

20
00:01:57.962 --> 00:02:00.396
I want to make sure I leave
on the perfect night.

21
00:02:00.498 --> 00:02:02.693
Kiki, wait!

22
00:02:06.471 --> 00:02:09.634
My, my.
What's this leaving business?

23
00:02:09.740 --> 00:02:11.935
It's one of our old customs.

24
00:02:12.043 --> 00:02:15.706
When a witch turns 13 she leaves home
for a year to begin her training.

25
00:02:16.547 --> 00:02:19.072
Your little baby is 13?

26
00:02:19.183 --> 00:02:22.050
My, my. Time flies so quickly,
doesn't it?

27
00:02:22.153 --> 00:02:25.213
I'm afraid so. But nobody
leaves home that young anymore.

28
00:02:25.990 --> 00:02:27.924
I remember perfectly well...

29
00:02:28.025 --> 00:02:31.222
the exact day
you arrived in this town.

30
00:02:31.329 --> 00:02:34.389
A little 13-year-old girl
came down from the sky...

31
00:02:34.499 --> 00:02:38.026
riding a broomstick,
her eyes shining.

32
00:02:38.135 --> 00:02:41.127
I thought you were
a bit stuck-up.

33
00:02:41.239 --> 00:02:43.639
But Kiki doesn't know much
besides flying.

34
00:02:43.741 --> 00:02:45.641
She hardly knows any
of my formulas.

35
00:02:46.310 --> 00:02:49.302
After I'm gone,
who will make this medicine?

36
00:02:49.413 --> 00:02:51.244
Sign of the times,
I'm afraid.

37
00:02:51.349 --> 00:02:53.340
Everything changes,
bit by bit.

38
00:02:53.451 --> 00:02:58.047
But I have to say,
nothing works as well for my rheumatism.

39
00:02:59.457 --> 00:03:03.393
You're always telling me to hurry!
Now who's the slowpoke?

40
00:03:03.494 --> 00:03:08.591
I think it's better to leave
with decorum and great dignity.

41
00:03:08.699 --> 00:03:13.261
If we put it off for a month, and I find
some wonderful boyfriend, then what?

42
00:03:13.371 --> 00:03:15.362
We'll never leave!

43
00:03:15.473 --> 00:03:18.442
I'm worried about this.
Once you've decided, you can't go back.

44
00:03:18.543 --> 00:03:20.738
Of course.
I know that.

45
00:03:20.845 --> 00:03:22.107
Good. It's there.

46
00:03:22.213 --> 00:03:25.580
I'm so excited!
It's like getting a birthday present!

47
00:03:30.521 --> 00:03:31.783
You won't believe it, Dad!

48
00:03:31.889 --> 00:03:34.414
I've decided
to go away tonight!

49
00:03:34.525 --> 00:03:37.289
- Tonight?
- Yeah! I just decided!

50
00:03:37.395 --> 00:03:41.297
Well, yes, but what about
our camping trip for this weekend?

51
00:03:41.399 --> 00:03:42.957
Sorry, Dad!

52
00:03:53.411 --> 00:03:56.812
Yes. I'll expect you then.
Thanks.

53
00:04:00.384 --> 00:04:03.979
Hi, Mom. I wanted to make sure
you knew that Kiki is leaving tonight.

54
00:04:04.088 --> 00:04:05.316
Yes, at midnight.

55
00:04:10.361 --> 00:04:14.127
- Not bad.
- I wish it were a different color.

56
00:04:14.231 --> 00:04:17.325
Witches have worn this color
for over a thousand years.

57
00:04:18.235 --> 00:04:20.829
Black cat, black clothes.

58
00:04:20.938 --> 00:04:23.668
It's not really important
what color your dress is.

59
00:04:23.774 --> 00:04:26.334
What matters is
the heart inside it.

60
00:04:26.444 --> 00:04:29.345
I know that having a good heart
is very important.

61
00:04:29.447 --> 00:04:32.177
I wish I could show you
that my heart is ready.

62
00:04:32.283 --> 00:04:34.342
Just follow that heart
and keep smiling.

63
00:04:34.452 --> 00:04:36.682
Okay.

64
00:04:36.787 --> 00:04:40.314
Be sure to write home
as soon as you've found a place.

65
00:04:41.459 --> 00:04:43.791
Dad, can I please
take the radio?

66
00:04:43.894 --> 00:04:46.192
Mom, you said
I could have his radio.

67
00:04:46.297 --> 00:04:49.630
<i>- Yea!
- Well, the radio's yours now.</i>

68
00:04:49.734 --> 00:04:53.135
Okay. Now let me have
a look at my little witch.

69
00:05:00.945 --> 00:05:03.004
You look just like your mother did
when she was your age.

70
00:05:03.114 --> 00:05:05.173
Dad...

71
00:05:05.282 --> 00:05:07.773
would you pick me up
like you used to?

72
00:05:07.885 --> 00:05:09.284
Well...

73
00:05:21.332 --> 00:05:25.200
How come you never told me
you were growing up so fast?

74
00:05:25.302 --> 00:05:28.203
You can always come home
if things don't work out.

75
00:05:28.305 --> 00:05:30.865
Come back to my old room?
No, thanks.

76
00:05:34.178 --> 00:05:36.078
I hope you find a good town.

77
00:05:47.625 --> 00:05:51.026
I bet it's real tough to find
a town to live in by yourself.

78
00:05:51.128 --> 00:05:53.028
Don't worry.
Kiki will be fine.

79
00:05:53.130 --> 00:05:56.190
- What kind of town are you looking for?
- A big town?

80
00:05:56.300 --> 00:05:58.825
Yeah.
By the ocean, I hope.

81
00:05:58.936 --> 00:06:01.837
- Wow!
- I'm so jealous of you!

82
00:06:01.939 --> 00:06:07.172
But I'm not going for a good time.
I'll be in training at least a year.

83
00:06:07.278 --> 00:06:10.179
Yeah, but they'll have discos,
won't they?

84
00:06:12.850 --> 00:06:15.580
- Kiki, it's almost time.
- Okay!

85
00:06:17.421 --> 00:06:19.321
That's the broom
you're leaving on?

86
00:06:19.423 --> 00:06:22.256
Yeah. I just made it.
Pretty cute, huh?

87
00:06:22.359 --> 00:06:26.557
It's cute, but you can't start witching
on a broom that's too small. Take mine.

88
00:06:26.664 --> 00:06:28.564
But, Mom, that one's so old.

89
00:06:28.666 --> 00:06:33.865
That's why you should have it.
It never loses its way, even in a storm.

90
00:06:33.971 --> 00:06:36.303
Kiki, trust me.

91
00:06:36.407 --> 00:06:39.638
But I worked so hard on it.
Right, Jiji?

92
00:06:39.744 --> 00:06:42.474
Your mother's broom would be better.

93
00:06:42.580 --> 00:06:44.275
You rotten traitor.

94
00:06:44.381 --> 00:06:49.785
He's right. You can make yourself
another broom when you get settled down.

95
00:06:56.227 --> 00:06:58.718
- Be careful.
- Go get 'em.

96
00:07:00.765 --> 00:07:04.428
- Bye!
- Have a good time!

97
00:07:09.006 --> 00:07:12.874
Go, go, Kiki!
Go, go, Kiki!

98
00:07:24.588 --> 00:07:26.522
She hasn't got the hang of it yet.

99
00:07:34.665 --> 00:07:37.725
She's well past the lake
and doing just fine.

100
00:07:37.835 --> 00:07:41.168
I'm going to miss the sound
of that little bell.

101
00:07:48.174 --> 00:07:49.732
Which way are we headed?

102
00:07:49.842 --> 00:07:51.935
I think south, to the ocean.

103
00:07:56.983 --> 00:08:01.352
Climb up and turn on the radio.
I don't think I can.

104
00:08:11.597 --> 00:08:17.263
KIKI'S DELIVERY SERVICE

105
00:08:18.371 --> 00:08:22.501
