113
00:09:17.797 --> 00:09:22.564
ANIMATION PRODUCTION Toru Hara
ASSOCIATE PRODUCER Toshio Suzuki

114
00:09:27.506 --> 00:09:31.101
PRODUCED, WRITTEN & DIRECTED by
Hayao Miyazaki

115
00:09:33.250 --> 00:09:36.913
- Good evening!
- It was.

116
00:09:38.355 --> 00:09:39.754
Newcomer, I suppose.

117
00:09:39.857 --> 00:09:42.257
I must be.
I just left home tonight.

118
00:09:43.527 --> 00:09:45.893
Would you mind
turning off that music?

119
00:09:45.996 --> 00:09:48.897
I prefer to fly
without accompaniment.

120
00:09:51.502 --> 00:09:55.268
Is it really hard to get settled
into a place you've never been?

121
00:09:56.373 --> 00:09:58.705
Oh, yes.
Lots can go wrong.

122
00:09:58.809 --> 00:10:02.267
But since I'm good at fortune-telling,
I can handle anything.

123
00:10:02.379 --> 00:10:03.607
Fortunes?

124
00:10:03.714 --> 00:10:07.115
In fact, I've started
telling fortunes about love lately.

125
00:10:07.217 --> 00:10:09.617
<i>What's your special skill?</i>

126
00:10:10.721 --> 00:10:13.155
I haven't made up my mind yet.

127
00:10:13.257 --> 00:10:16.420
Uh-huh. Well, I'm nearly finished
with my training period.

128
00:10:16.527 --> 00:10:19.428
It'll be terrific
to go home with confidence.

129
00:10:19.530 --> 00:10:21.589
That's my town down there.

130
00:10:23.133 --> 00:10:26.364
It's not big or terribly interesting,
but I like it.

131
00:10:26.470 --> 00:10:28.870
- Good luck to you.
- Thanks.

132
00:10:30.574 --> 00:10:31.632
Good-bye!

133
00:10:35.512 --> 00:10:38.811
Disgusting.
What a stuck-up cat.

134
00:10:39.917 --> 00:10:41.748
I have to have a special skill.

135
00:10:46.223 --> 00:10:48.919
What was that about good weather?

136
00:10:58.535 --> 00:11:01.129
I hope you're not going to do
what I think you're going to do.

137
00:11:12.516 --> 00:11:15.041
We'll sleep here
until the storm's gone.

138
00:11:15.152 --> 00:11:18.053
- Won't we get into trouble?
- Not if nobody finds us.

139
00:11:24.161 --> 00:11:26.220
I'm soaked through.

140
00:11:26.330 --> 00:11:28.457
Do you feel anything moving?

141
00:11:31.869 --> 00:11:33.769
This smells great.

142
00:12:49.746 --> 00:12:52.510
Sorry. We didn't mean to fall asleep
in your breakfast.

143
00:13:04.161 --> 00:13:06.823
Jiji, you've gotta
come see the ocean.

144
00:13:06.930 --> 00:13:08.420
I don't believe it!
It's huge!

145
00:13:08.532 --> 00:13:12.628
- It's only a puddle to me.
- Aw, come on.

146
00:13:21.812 --> 00:13:25.578
That one's giant. Think there
might be other witches there?

147
00:13:25.682 --> 00:13:26.808
How would I know?

148
00:13:41.264 --> 00:13:42.663
Let's go!

149
00:13:52.242 --> 00:13:54.142
You all right back there?

150
00:13:55.245 --> 00:13:58.646
Look.
A big town by the sea.

151
00:14:27.310 --> 00:14:31.110
Can you believe my luck?
A clock tower and everything!

152
00:14:31.214 --> 00:14:33.774
<i>What if there are
some witches living here?</i>

153
00:14:33.884 --> 00:14:35.181
There may not be.

154
00:15:12.522 --> 00:15:16.754
- Am I gonna like it here!
- It's a trifle large for my taste.

155
00:15:16.860 --> 00:15:20.694
Bless my hourglass!
If that ain't a witch!

156
00:15:21.765 --> 00:15:23.062
Good morning!

157
00:15:23.166 --> 00:15:25.498
Are there any other witches
in this town?

158
00:15:25.602 --> 00:15:29.504
No. Can't say as I've seen
a single one of'em lately.

159
00:15:29.606 --> 00:15:33.042
How about that? Our trip is over.
We're gonna settle down right here.

160
00:15:33.143 --> 00:15:35.839
- Thanks, mister! Bye!
- Don't mention it!

161
00:15:40.517 --> 00:15:43.418
- Tell me we're not landing down there.
- Of course we are.

162
00:15:55.532 --> 00:15:57.159
Everybody's looking at us.

163
00:15:57.267 --> 00:16:00.532
I know. Smile and make
a good first impression.

164
00:16:40.777 --> 00:16:43.803
Well, you see, I'm a witch.
My name is Kiki.

165
00:16:43.914 --> 00:16:46.075
This is my black cat Jiji.

166
00:16:46.183 --> 00:16:48.583
We'd be honored
if we could live here.

167
00:16:52.155 --> 00:16:55.852
We'd love to live here.
You have a wonderful bell tower.

168
00:16:57.827 --> 00:17:00.728
We're glad you like it, my dear.
Bye!

169
00:17:08.905 --> 00:17:11.999
Hey, kid, what were you doing
jumping into the street like that?

170
00:17:12.108 --> 00:17:14.008
You almost caused an accident.

171
00:17:14.110 --> 00:17:17.011
You must be crazy,
zooming around on a broom in public.

172
00:17:17.113 --> 00:17:20.014
I'm a new witch, sir.
We're supposed to fly around.

173
00:17:20.116 --> 00:17:23.017
You're supposed to obey the law
the same as other people.

174
00:17:23.119 --> 00:17:25.019
What's your name and address?

175
00:17:25.121 --> 00:17:29.023
- Are you gonna tell my parents?
- Of course, if it's necessary.

176
00:17:29.125 --> 00:17:31.025
I have to.
You're a minor.

177
00:17:31.127 --> 00:17:34.290
Thief! Somebody stop him!
Stop, thief!

178
00:17:34.397 --> 00:17:36.524
Don't you move from there!

179
00:17:59.990 --> 00:18:01.548
Kiki.

180
00:18:04.427 --> 00:18:07.328
Wait up!
It worked out pretty good, huh?

181
00:18:07.430 --> 00:18:12.697
Good plan to get rid of that cop, huh?
I was the one yelling "Thief!"

182
00:18:12.802 --> 00:18:15.236
You're a real witch, right?

183
00:18:15.338 --> 00:18:17.829
Could I look at that broom?

184
00:18:17.941 --> 00:18:22.275
Hey, Tombo! Isn't it a bit early
for girl hunting?

185
00:18:22.379 --> 00:18:24.677
Hey, you guys, shut up.

186
00:18:28.251 --> 00:18:32.051
Let me look at your broom.
Please? Just for a minute.

187
00:18:32.155 --> 00:18:33.952
I didn't ask for your help.

188
00:18:34.057 --> 00:18:35.957
I guess I have to thank you...

189
00:18:36.059 --> 00:18:40.496
but it was rude for you to do something
without introducing yourself.

190
00:18:51.274 --> 00:18:54.175
How old-fashioned.
You sound like my grandma.

191
00:18:54.277 --> 00:18:56.177
Go away and leave me alone!

192
00:19:06.856 --> 00:19:08.323
What a cool witch.

193
00:19:12.595 --> 00:19:16.656
Stay here alone? I don't understand.
Aren't your parents here with you?

194
00:19:16.766 --> 00:19:20.964
No. I'm a witch, so since I'm 13, I'm
supposed to be completely independent.

195
00:19:21.071 --> 00:19:23.266
May I see some identification?

196
00:19:24.207 --> 00:19:26.107
Never mind then.

197
00:19:39.989 --> 00:19:43.891
- Are you going to eat that?
- You can have it.

198
00:19:46.963 --> 00:19:49.864
It's going to be getting dark
fairly soon.

199
00:19:57.207 --> 00:19:58.765
Let's go.

200
00:20:36.746 --> 00:20:40.238
Let's just find another town.
There must be plenty of nice ones.

201
00:20:40.350 --> 00:20:42.978
Perhaps one
even bigger than this one.

202
00:20:49.726 --> 00:20:52.559
Lady! Your pacifier!

203
00:20:52.662 --> 00:20:54.789
Lady, you forgot this!

204
00:20:58.768 --> 00:21:03.603
When that baby wakes up
and doesn't find this, she's gonna cry.

205
00:21:09.012 --> 00:21:13.506
I'm sorry, sir, but could you wait
just a minute? I'll be right back.

206
00:21:17.487 --> 00:21:21.719
- I could bring it down to her.
- What?

207
00:21:21.825 --> 00:21:25.852
The woman with the baby carriage, right?
It'd be easy. I'd really like to.

208
00:21:25.962 --> 00:21:27.930
That'd be a big help.

209
00:21:28.031 --> 00:21:30.295
- Thank you very much.
- My pleasure.

210
00:21:31.401 --> 00:21:33.392
Let's go, Jiji.

211
00:21:42.512 --> 00:21:43.979
Wow!

212
00:21:53.823 --> 00:21:57.156
Sorry to startle you, but
you left this pacifier in the bakery.

213
00:22:14.143 --> 00:22:16.407
Here you go.

214
00:22:16.513 --> 00:22:20.040
- I'd like one of those.
- Sure. Hi! Come on in.

215
00:22:27.090 --> 00:22:28.751
Thank you.

216
00:22:29.826 --> 00:22:31.259
Thank you.

217
00:22:32.529 --> 00:22:33.928
Bye.

218
00:22:37.367 --> 00:22:39.267
There you are.

219
00:22:44.073 --> 00:22:47.531
I must say, I nearly fainted
when I saw you fly off.

220
00:22:47.644 --> 00:22:51.011
That woman told me
to give you this message right away.

221
00:22:53.616 --> 00:22:55.516
"I got the pacifier you sent.

222
00:22:55.618 --> 00:22:59.110
Be sure to thank your little friend.
She's an absolute angel."

223
00:22:59.222 --> 00:23:01.281
I'm glad I could help you out.
Bye!

224
00:23:01.391 --> 00:23:05.657
Where are you going so fast?
Have something to drink.

225
00:23:12.001 --> 00:23:13.901
Come up here.

226
00:23:18.608 --> 00:23:21.509
Sit down and relax.
I'll make some hot chocolate.

227
00:23:35.325 --> 00:23:38.226
- Thank you very much.
- And this is for you.

228
00:23:40.763 --> 00:23:43.994
Let me guess.
You're a witch in training.

229
00:23:46.169 --> 00:23:49.536
Yes, but people don't seem
fond of witches in this town.

230
00:23:49.639 --> 00:23:52.836
There are many kinds of people
in this town who will like you.

231
00:23:52.942 --> 00:23:56.105
Take me, for instance.
I like you very much.

232
00:23:57.981 --> 00:24:00.040
Found a place to stay yet?

233
00:24:04.420 --> 00:24:06.888
You should have told me
you hadn't.

234
00:24:06.990 --> 00:24:09.891
We have a vacant room in the attic
you can stay in.

235
00:24:09.993 --> 00:24:12.257
You'd give me a room?

236
00:24:13.496 --> 00:24:14.929
I'd be happy to.

237
00:24:15.031 --> 00:24:17.522
Let me introduce myself.
I'm Osono.

238
00:24:18.501 --> 00:24:19.866
My name's Kiki.

239
00:24:19.969 --> 00:24:22.028
This is my black cat Jiji.

240
00:24:36.285 --> 00:24:38.753
It's not very clean at the moment,
but it's all yours.

241
00:24:38.855 --> 00:24:39.913
Thank you.

242
00:24:40.023 --> 00:24:41.752
Bathroom and water
are downstairs.

243
00:24:41.858 --> 00:24:44.759
- Don't hesitate to ask for anything.
- Thank you!

244
00:24:49.532 --> 00:24:51.432
There's flour everywhere.

245
00:25:04.313 --> 00:25:07.441
At this rate,
I'll be a white cat by morning.

246
00:25:11.320 --> 00:25:14.585
Jiji, come look
at the ocean from here.

247
00:25:20.630 --> 00:25:23.531
Shall we try to find
another town?

248
00:25:28.838 --> 00:25:30.772
<i>The Freedom Adventurer...</i>

249
00:25:30.873 --> 00:25:32.602
<i>sponsored by the World Airship
Popularization Association...</i>

250
00:25:32.709 --> 00:25:34.643
<i>has commenced its maiden voyage
to Antarctica.</i>

251
00:25:36.212 --> 00:25:38.146
What a snob she is.

252
00:25:55.665 --> 00:25:58.065
I've decided
not to leave this town.

253
00:25:58.167 --> 00:26:01.068
Maybe I can find others
like Osono...

254
00:26:01.170 --> 00:26:04.571
who will like me and accept me
for what I am.

255
00:27:58.454 --> 00:28:01.355
How much do you think a phone
would cost to put in here?

256
00:28:01.457 --> 00:28:04.790
- A phone?
- Yeah. For my business.

257
00:28:26.115 --> 00:28:27.514
Good morning, everyone.

258
00:28:27.617 --> 00:28:29.915
- Did you sleep well?
- Yes!

259
00:28:30.019 --> 00:28:32.920
That smells good.
Can I help out?

260
00:28:54.577 --> 00:28:57.068
A delivery service, huh?

261
00:28:57.179 --> 00:29:02.014
I have one skill... flying... so I thought
a delivery service was a good idea.

262
00:29:02.118 --> 00:29:05.519
Everyone will love it.
Kiki's Flying Delivery Service.

263
00:29:05.621 --> 00:29:10.024
And you can base the business out of
your room upstairs if you want to.

264
00:29:10.126 --> 00:29:13.254
"If I want to"?
Oh, boy!

265
00:29:13.362 --> 00:29:16.695
- I'd like to put a phone up there.
- But a phone costs money.

266
00:29:16.799 --> 00:29:19.927
- I have some saved up already.
- Don't waste it.

267
00:29:20.803 --> 00:29:23.363
Why not use our phone?

268
00:29:23.472 --> 00:29:25.940
It takes time
to get regular customers.

269
00:29:26.042 --> 00:29:30.308
If you help around the bakery, you won't
have to pay rent or the phone bill.

270
00:29:30.413 --> 00:29:32.938
I need a lot of help
since I'm expecting a baby.

271
00:29:33.049 --> 00:29:35.279
And I'll throw in
free breakfast too.

272
00:29:35.384 --> 00:29:37.409
Thank you!

273
00:29:37.520 --> 00:29:39.784
I'll do my very best for you.

274
00:29:41.724 --> 00:29:43.624
You're such a wonderful person!

275
00:30:15.057 --> 00:30:17.582
Jiji, come on!
I'm all done!

276
00:30:19.528 --> 00:30:21.428
It's time to go shopping.

277
00:30:37.279 --> 00:30:40.646
Stop jumping out into the street.
We're not at home.

278
00:30:40.750 --> 00:30:43.014
I'm sorry.
I won't do it again.

279
00:30:44.120 --> 00:30:48.079
I've never been more embarrassed
in my whole life.

280
00:30:48.190 --> 00:30:49.851
It was so terrible!

281
00:30:59.268 --> 00:31:03.329
I wish I had something pretty to wear
besides this robe.

282
00:31:12.581 --> 00:31:14.310
Boy, this is expensive.

283
00:31:14.417 --> 00:31:16.647
Kiki, look! It's me!

284
00:31:29.598 --> 00:31:32.499
- Do you have any money left?
- A little.

285
00:31:32.601 --> 00:31:35.502
We'll just have to eat
a lot of pancakes for a while.

286
00:31:46.982 --> 00:31:50.076
Wow!
Those are beautiful.

287
00:31:56.992 --> 00:31:59.392
Wait!
Pull over a second!

288
00:32:00.496 --> 00:32:03.090
Hey, yo! Miss Witch!
Turn around!

289
00:32:04.333 --> 00:32:06.096
Nice goin', Tombo!

290
00:32:06.202 --> 00:32:07.863
Not flying today?

291
00:32:09.805 --> 00:32:12.740
What'd I tell you?
Black is all she wears.

292
00:32:12.842 --> 00:32:15.902
Wait! Come back! I'm sorry!
I was only kidding!

293
00:32:29.091 --> 00:32:30.456
Perfect timing, Kiki.

294
00:32:30.559 --> 00:32:34.120
A lady wants you to deliver something.
She's your first customer.

295
00:32:34.230 --> 00:32:36.562
Customer?
I'll be right back!

296
00:32:41.070 --> 00:32:42.970
The map!

297
00:32:53.916 --> 00:32:56.248
This lady is a customer of ours.

298
00:32:56.352 --> 00:32:59.116
We were talking about
your delivery service.

299
00:32:59.221 --> 00:33:02.213
- You are a cute little witch.
- My name's Kiki, ma'am.

300
00:33:02.324 --> 00:33:06.158
I've heard wonderful things about you.
Could you deliver this by tonight?

301
00:33:07.296 --> 00:33:10.424
- Yes!
- It's my nephew's birthday.

302
00:33:10.533 --> 00:33:14.435
An urgent job came up, so I can't get
there myself to give him his present.

303
00:33:14.537 --> 00:33:16.505
Where do you want it delivered?

304
00:33:19.275 --> 00:33:20.435
That's me.

305
00:33:21.243 --> 00:33:23.143
It won't be too far?

306
00:33:23.245 --> 00:33:25.338
I can fly there
directly from here.

307
00:33:25.447 --> 00:33:29.008
- How much do you want?
- I haven't really set a price yet.

308
00:33:30.419 --> 00:33:31.681
Is this enough?

309
00:33:36.225 --> 00:33:39.092
This is more than enough.
Thank you very much, ma'am.

310
00:34:03.586 --> 00:34:05.611
Oh, wow! That's great!

311
00:34:05.721 --> 00:34:09.987
- I certainly wish I could fly.
- Yeah! Hey, do you know that girl?

312
00:34:28.410 --> 00:34:31.174
How high do you intend to go?

313
00:34:31.280 --> 00:34:35.182
It's my first delivery. I don't want
to be stopped by that police officer.

314
00:34:36.518 --> 00:34:40.420
I was afraid you were going to
deliver it to the angels.

315
00:34:46.228 --> 00:34:49.129
I'm guessing
it's just beyond the cape.

316
00:34:50.466 --> 00:34:52.366
Here we go!

317
00:35:00.142 --> 00:35:02.337
I'm liking this town
more and more.

318
00:35:02.444 --> 00:35:04.378
I'm not sure what I think.

319
00:35:04.480 --> 00:35:07.347
I'll finally be able
to write Mom.

320
00:35:26.168 --> 00:35:28.796
Those are wild geese.
Wonderful!

321
00:35:31.206 --> 00:35:33.606
They're flying along with us!

322
00:35:59.068 --> 00:36:02.401
- They seem awfully upset.
- They say a wind's coming.

323
00:36:02.504 --> 00:36:04.995
They also say
they're going higher.

324
00:36:42.111 --> 00:36:44.602
I'm sorry. L... Oww!

325
00:36:48.717 --> 00:36:52.585
Please! I'm sorry!
I wasn't trying to steal your eggs!

326
00:37:01.530 --> 00:37:03.430
I've never been so scared.

327
00:37:03.532 --> 00:37:07.434
It's your fault. They warned us
of that wind, but you didn't listen.

328
00:37:07.536 --> 00:37:08.798
You're right.

329
00:37:12.174 --> 00:37:16.042
That's beautiful. They were able
to fly that high up with the wind.

330
00:37:16.145 --> 00:37:18.170
Kiki!

331
00:37:18.280 --> 00:37:19.713
The toy is gone!

332
00:37:21.517 --> 00:37:23.576
We've gotta go back
to where we fell!

333
00:37:37.666 --> 00:37:40.430
They're saying,
"The egg thief's coming again!"

334
00:37:40.536 --> 00:37:42.436
What are we gonna do?

335
00:37:58.620 --> 00:38:00.247
Hey! Stop that!

336
00:38:00.355 --> 00:38:02.448
Don't do that!

337
00:38:02.558 --> 00:38:04.458
Stop it!

338
00:38:16.705 --> 00:38:18.764
We're in trouble.
They're still upset.

339
00:38:18.874 --> 00:38:21.604
Witches get no respect these days.

340
00:38:21.710 --> 00:38:24.270
Crows used to be
witches' servants.

341
00:38:24.379 --> 00:38:27.610
That was a long time ago, okay?

342
00:38:27.716 --> 00:38:31.675
How about we go in after the forest
is dark, get it and get out?

343
00:38:31.787 --> 00:38:34.278
We'll never make it in time.

344
00:38:34.389 --> 00:38:36.721
There's only one way to do it.

345
00:38:36.825 --> 00:38:38.725
They'll find out I'm a fake.

346
00:38:38.827 --> 00:38:42.058
After I find it,
I'll be right back to help you out.

347
00:38:45.767 --> 00:38:48.099
- Is that the place?
- Yes. Don't move a muscle.

348
00:38:48.203 --> 00:38:50.763
- Can I breathe?
- Hold it as long as you can.

349
00:39:08.223 --> 00:39:10.350
Yea!
Give me my present!

350
00:39:13.629 --> 00:39:15.529
That's pretty weird.

351
00:39:20.636 --> 00:39:22.035
A bit late, aren't you?

352
00:39:22.137 --> 00:39:25.038
After my sister telephoned,
we were wondering where you were.

353
00:39:25.140 --> 00:39:27.631
I'm sorry. Oh.

354
00:39:30.546 --> 00:39:32.639
Could I please have
your signature?

355
00:39:33.715 --> 00:39:36.240
Mom, can I put
the canaries in here?

356
00:39:36.351 --> 00:39:39.752
Uh-huh, but be careful
you don't let any of them escape.

357
00:39:39.855 --> 00:39:41.516
Okay.

358
00:39:43.825 --> 00:39:46.555
Thank you very much.
Have a nice day.

359
00:39:56.638 --> 00:39:59.334
Come on, birdie!

360
00:39:59.441 --> 00:40:02.706
I'm gonna put you
in a bigger house!

361
00:40:06.348 --> 00:40:07.975
Please hurry, Kiki.

362
00:40:38.146 --> 00:40:42.048
I know it was here,
so it's gotta be around someplace.

363
00:40:55.864 --> 00:40:57.263
There it is!

364
00:41:02.004 --> 00:41:04.131
Excuse me! Anybody home?

365
00:41:04.239 --> 00:41:07.037
Can you please help me?
Anybody?

366
00:41:14.349 --> 00:41:15.907
Anybody here?

367
00:41:16.018 --> 00:41:20.148
Yeah!
I can't come down right now.

368
00:41:21.323 --> 00:41:23.314
Why don't you come up?

369
00:41:34.436 --> 00:41:35.630
What do you want?

370
00:41:35.737 --> 00:41:39.503
That stuffed black cat
you put behind your window?

371
00:41:39.608 --> 00:41:41.405
I'm sorry, but it's mine.
I dropped it.

372
00:41:43.011 --> 00:41:45.502
Be good,
and don't move yet.

373
00:41:48.183 --> 00:41:50.413
I found it in the forest.

374
00:41:50.519 --> 00:41:53.852
Would you give it back
to me, please?

375
00:41:53.955 --> 00:41:56.924
Hang on a minute.
I can't stop just now.

376
00:41:57.025 --> 00:41:58.993
Nice. Very nice.

377
00:42:00.362 --> 00:42:02.694
You're beautiful
just the way you are.

378
00:42:11.540 --> 00:42:14.634
You really should have told me
you were in a hurry.

379
00:42:17.546 --> 00:42:20.014
- I got sort of fond of it.
- I'm sorry.

380
00:42:23.418 --> 00:42:25.318
The stuffing's coming out.

381
00:42:25.420 --> 00:42:28.321
I'll bet the crows did it.
They were making a big fuss over it.

382
00:42:28.423 --> 00:42:31.324
What am I gonna do?
I can't deliver it like this.

383
00:42:33.428 --> 00:42:36.591
Say!
How about we work out a deal?

384
00:42:38.567 --> 00:42:41.161
That's pretty exciting.
And at 13 too.

385
00:42:42.270 --> 00:42:44.761
To be completely independent.
That's great.

386
00:42:44.873 --> 00:42:47.808
- Can you fix it?
- Trust me.

387
00:42:55.016 --> 00:42:56.916
Ketto, time for your bath.

388
00:42:59.621 --> 00:43:03.682
Quickly! The guests
will be here soon!

389
00:43:06.228 --> 00:43:07.627
Ketto!

390
00:44:06.721 --> 00:44:09.622
- I'm done.
- Thank you so much!

391
00:44:09.724 --> 00:44:12.124
You'd better help Jiji
before it's too late.

392
00:44:12.227 --> 00:44:15.958
- But I haven't finished yet.
- You've done enough. Go help him.

393
00:44:16.064 --> 00:44:17.622
Thanks!

394
00:44:28.317 --> 00:44:31.047
Jeff likes my present
more than me!

395
00:44:31.153 --> 00:44:32.677
It is strange, you know.

396
00:44:32.788 --> 00:44:35.985
He adores that stuffed cat.
He won't leave it alone.

397
00:44:36.091 --> 00:44:37.991
He thinks it's a puppy.

398
00:44:38.093 --> 00:44:41.221
Your sister's not going to be
happy to hear that.

399
00:44:41.330 --> 00:44:45.198
- That's okay. I gave it to Jeff anyway.
- Remember to tell Auntie "thank you."

400
00:44:46.635 --> 00:44:51.937
You should be nicer to him.
Jeff is a very old dog.

401
00:44:52.041 --> 00:44:54.669
But, Grandma,
all he does is sleep!

402
00:44:54.777 --> 00:44:56.677
I suppose that's true.

403
00:44:57.780 --> 00:45:00.874
Ketto, go open the door.
Jeff wants to go out.

404
00:45:02.885 --> 00:45:05.786
Be sure to push the door shut
when you're finished.

405
00:45:14.897 --> 00:45:17.388
- Jiji!
- Kiki, what took you so long?

406
00:45:17.499 --> 00:45:18.761
I'm sorry.

407
00:45:18.867 --> 00:45:21.529
That marvelous dog
helped me escape.

408
00:45:27.443 --> 00:45:30.844
He said he'd be happy
to help us out if he could.

409
00:45:37.319 --> 00:45:39.719
Would you take this back in?

410
00:46:09.618 --> 00:46:11.210
What's the matter?

411
00:46:11.320 --> 00:46:13.550
- I'm famished.
- Yeah, me too.

412
00:46:13.655 --> 00:46:15.555
And I'm tired too.

413
00:46:15.657 --> 00:46:17.887
But it sure was
a wonderful adventure.

414
00:46:17.993 --> 00:46:22.760
And that painter who found the stuffed
cat wants to do a drawing with me in it.

415
00:46:22.865 --> 00:46:24.492
- Naked?
- Don't be silly!

416
00:46:35.411 --> 00:46:38.380
"Kiki's Delivery Service"

417
00:47:59.540 --> 00:48:01.440
Boring.

418
00:48:09.950 --> 00:48:12.851
What are you doing?
You're supposed to be minding the shop.

419
00:48:12.953 --> 00:48:15.854
I am,
but nobody's coming in today.

420
00:48:15.956 --> 00:48:21.360
- But it always gets busy around now.
- I know, but that's not what I mean.

421
00:48:21.462 --> 00:48:23.225
<i>I mean my customers.</i>

422
00:48:23.330 --> 00:48:27.460
Jiji, if nobody comes in
I'll have to eat pancakes forever...

423
00:48:27.568 --> 00:48:30.401
and be fat, fat, fat!

424
00:48:30.504 --> 00:48:32.904
So, what am I supposed to do?

425
00:48:33.007 --> 00:48:36.909
I think pancakes are superb,
providing they're not burned, of course.

426
00:48:37.011 --> 00:48:41.448
You're no help.
When you get fat, see if I care.

427
00:48:48.389 --> 00:48:51.950
Beautiful, isn't she? Somebody told me
she's a fashion designer.

428
00:48:52.059 --> 00:48:55.324
Personally, I'm not very fond
of her conceited cat.

429
00:48:58.699 --> 00:49:01.031
Hello. Gutiokipan Bakery.

430
00:49:01.135 --> 00:49:03.626
Pardon? Yes, ma'am.

431
00:49:03.737 --> 00:49:06.365
About time we got a customer.

432
00:49:06.473 --> 00:49:09.840
4:30 will be a perfect time
to pick it up. If you'll just...

433
00:49:09.943 --> 00:49:12.411
Uh-huh. And the address?

434
00:49:12.513 --> 00:49:15.346
Yes. The blue roof.
Right.

435
00:49:15.449 --> 00:49:17.679
Yes, I'm sure I have it all.

436
00:49:17.785 --> 00:49:19.776
Thank you very much.

437
00:49:22.956 --> 00:49:24.856
Hi.

438
00:49:32.599 --> 00:49:34.032
I'll take this one.

439
00:49:35.135 --> 00:49:36.534
Okay?

440
00:49:41.975 --> 00:49:43.875
Thank you very much.
Good afternoon.

441
00:49:43.977 --> 00:49:46.070
Are you still mad at me?

442
00:49:46.180 --> 00:49:48.546
We're having a party
at the club tonight.

443
00:49:48.649 --> 00:49:52.949
It's called the flying club,
and we'd really like you to come.

444
00:49:53.053 --> 00:49:55.453
Here's your invitation.

445
00:49:58.425 --> 00:50:00.723
It really is a serious club.

446
00:50:00.828 --> 00:50:03.729
Everybody would be very happy
if you came.

447
00:50:03.831 --> 00:50:05.355
May I help you?

448
00:50:05.466 --> 00:50:08.367
They tell me
you have a delivery service.

449
00:50:08.469 --> 00:50:10.937
Oh. Pardon me.
Yes, of course we do.

450
00:50:11.038 --> 00:50:14.235
It's urgent this package arrive tonight.
Can you do it?

451
00:50:14.341 --> 00:50:16.673
Of course we can...

452
00:50:16.777 --> 00:50:18.404
Are you gonna be all right?

453
00:50:18.512 --> 00:50:20.377
- Uh-huh.
- Can I help you?

454
00:50:20.481 --> 00:50:21.880
Uh-uh.

455
00:50:37.397 --> 00:50:41.299
I'll be back at 6:00,
so make up your mind by then.

456
00:50:41.869 --> 00:50:43.234
How much will that be?

457
00:50:43.337 --> 00:50:46.033
Will that be inside
or outside the city limits?

458
00:50:46.140 --> 00:50:49.598
- I wrote it down on the box.
- The box? Oh, I'm sorry.

459
00:50:53.013 --> 00:50:54.537
Osono!

460
00:50:54.648 --> 00:50:58.015
I got an invitation to a party
at Tombo's flying club.

461
00:50:58.118 --> 00:51:00.052
Terrific!
You'll have a wonderful time.

462
00:51:00.154 --> 00:51:02.554
But what am I gonna wear?

463
00:51:02.656 --> 00:51:06.854
Kiki, I wouldn't worry too much.
You look fine in that.

464
00:51:06.960 --> 00:51:09.292
It makes you look beautiful
and mysterious.

465
00:51:09.396 --> 00:51:11.728
- You mean it?
- Any work yet?

466
00:51:11.832 --> 00:51:14.960
I almost forgot about it!
It's already 4:00!

467
00:51:15.068 --> 00:51:16.763
Oh, no!

468
00:51:16.870 --> 00:51:20.738
Can you watch the store
till I get back? Jiji! Jiji!

469
00:51:37.090 --> 00:51:40.753
Why are you going to this party
when you're so mad at him?

470
00:51:40.861 --> 00:51:44.797
I have to concentrate.
This thing is so heavy. Be quiet.

471
00:52:03.951 --> 00:52:05.384
Thank you.

472
00:52:06.520 --> 00:52:07.919
Come on!

473
00:52:12.092 --> 00:52:14.993
Our next appointment is at 4:30.

474
00:52:28.742 --> 00:52:30.869
There's the blue roof.

475
00:52:49.563 --> 00:52:54.466
My name's Kiki. Someone telephoned
for a delivery service, so here I am.

476
00:52:54.568 --> 00:52:56.468
Right this way, dear.

477
00:53:02.309 --> 00:53:05.608
- You're right on time.
- Yes, ma'am.

478
00:53:09.316 --> 00:53:12.649
Madam, the delivery girl is here.

479
00:53:13.754 --> 00:53:16.245
What? Oh, my goodness.
Is it that time already?

480
00:53:16.356 --> 00:53:18.415
What a pleasant surprise.

481
00:53:18.525 --> 00:53:20.720
Please make yourself at home,
my dear.

482
00:53:20.827 --> 00:53:22.795
- Come, come.
- Thanks.

483
00:53:22.896 --> 00:53:24.796
May I take that for you?

484
00:53:33.540 --> 00:53:35.440
Broom and black cat.

485
00:53:35.542 --> 00:53:38.739
It's just like my great-grandmother
always told me.

486
00:53:39.947 --> 00:53:42.313
My name is Kiki,
and I'm a witch.

487
00:53:43.583 --> 00:53:46.677
Oh, but what a cute
little girl you are.

488
00:53:46.787 --> 00:53:52.157
I'm so sorry, but that pie you were
supposed to deliver isn't ready yet.

489
00:53:54.361 --> 00:53:57.455
The temperature
doesn't seem to go up at all.

490
00:53:57.564 --> 00:53:58.895
Something's wrong.

491
00:54:01.234 --> 00:54:05.568
Machines don't work
when they become old like me.

492
00:54:05.672 --> 00:54:09.631
I was hoping you could deliver it hot
to my grandchild's birthday party.

493
00:54:09.743 --> 00:54:14.612
It's one of my favorite recipes:
Herring and pumpkin pie.

494
00:54:14.715 --> 00:54:17.115
I guess I have to admit defeat.

495
00:54:17.217 --> 00:54:19.981
I'll have to phone her
and tell her I'm sorry.

496
00:54:20.087 --> 00:54:23.318
I feel just awful
having you come here for nothing.

497
00:54:23.423 --> 00:54:26.415
Bertha!

498
00:54:28.061 --> 00:54:30.427
Would you get her money, please.

499
00:54:30.530 --> 00:54:31.895
Certainly, ma'am.

500
00:54:31.999 --> 00:54:34.695
All of it.
Pay her the amount we agreed on.

501
00:54:34.801 --> 00:54:37.497
- Oh, no. Please!
- Now, don't be silly.

502
00:54:37.604 --> 00:54:39.663
It's not your fault
it wasn't ready.

503
00:54:42.309 --> 00:54:44.971
I have no other jobs today.
Maybe I could help.

504
00:54:45.078 --> 00:54:46.978
Does that oven over there work?

505
00:54:47.080 --> 00:54:49.571
You mean that one?

506
00:54:51.351 --> 00:54:55.481
It used to be the only one I ever used,
but I haven't opened it in years.

507
00:54:55.589 --> 00:55:00.288
If it burns firewood, I can help.
I used to help my mom all the time.

508
00:55:00.394 --> 00:55:02.760
It's a big job to build a fire.

509
00:55:02.863 --> 00:55:04.763
It's a great idea, madam.

510
00:55:04.865 --> 00:55:08.528
I never did like that electric thing,
and we have plenty of firewood.

511
00:55:08.635 --> 00:55:10.000
I can build a fire.

512
00:55:10.103 --> 00:55:14.540
Well, I'm not sure,
but if you think you can build it...

513
00:55:19.179 --> 00:55:22.171
<i>Have you considered that this might
make you late for your party?</i>

514
00:55:22.282 --> 00:55:24.147
I can't take money for nothing.

515
00:55:32.259 --> 00:55:34.159
Come on.
We have to hurry up.

516
00:55:35.796 --> 00:55:38.492
Look what I found.
And it works!

517
00:55:38.598 --> 00:55:42.864
You're very good at this, my dear.
Your mother taught you well.

518
00:55:52.345 --> 00:55:54.711
Oh, my goodness,
it's so exciting.

519
00:55:54.815 --> 00:55:57.750
Never did like electricity.

520
00:56:12.165 --> 00:56:14.065
It should be about time.

521
00:56:14.167 --> 00:56:16.101
Yes, very good.
Well done.

522
00:56:27.314 --> 00:56:29.145
And now we wait.

523
00:56:29.249 --> 00:56:32.150
- About 40 minutes or so. Right?
- Exactly right.

524
00:56:32.252 --> 00:56:36.621
- So why don't we take a little break?
- Do you need help with anything else?

525
00:56:36.723 --> 00:56:40.625
Oh! Well,
if you'd really like to...

526
00:56:41.728 --> 00:56:43.093
Thanks very much.

527
00:56:43.196 --> 00:56:45.187
You're very welcome.

528
00:56:46.199 --> 00:56:50.033
- You're going to be late for the party.
- Stop worrying.

529
00:56:50.137 --> 00:56:53.436
It'll only take me 15 minutes
if I fly there fast.

530
00:56:54.808 --> 00:56:57.971
Would you care for some tea?
I just made it fresh.

531
00:57:00.113 --> 00:57:02.775
I just remembered.
Won't you be late for your party?

532
00:57:02.883 --> 00:57:05.977
It won't be a problem.
It'll take me 15 minutes from here.

533
00:57:07.754 --> 00:57:11.690
But, my dear, that clock
runs about ten minutes slow.

534
00:57:11.791 --> 00:57:15.022
- What'll I do?
- See if the pie's ready.

535
00:57:16.163 --> 00:57:17.994
Bertha! Bertha!

536
00:57:26.940 --> 00:57:31.104
- Is the pie ready?
- It smells fine, so you'd better hurry.

537
00:57:39.686 --> 00:57:40.744
Better hurry!
Come on!

538
00:57:40.854 --> 00:57:44.017
- Okay.
- Don't forget your money.

539
00:57:44.124 --> 00:57:47.025
- That's way too much.
- Not for what you've done.

540
00:57:47.127 --> 00:57:49.357
Hurry up, Kiki,
or you'll be late!

541
00:57:50.463 --> 00:57:53.091
- Have a good time!
- Be careful!

542
00:57:59.739 --> 00:58:02.173
What happened
to all that good weather?

543
00:58:02.275 --> 00:58:04.140
My whiskers are tingling.

544
00:58:28.001 --> 00:58:32.404
- Could we get out of the rain?
- We can't! That'll only make us later!

545
00:58:32.505 --> 00:58:34.405
Besides, the food will get cold
if we stop.

546
00:59:37.604 --> 00:59:38.866
Yes?

547
00:59:38.972 --> 00:59:40.837
I have a delivery.

548
00:59:40.940 --> 00:59:42.430
But it's completely wet.

549
00:59:42.542 --> 00:59:47.138
I'm sorry. It began to rain on the way.
But the food came through all right.

550
00:59:47.247 --> 00:59:50.375
I told Grandma
I didn't want that.

551
00:59:50.483 --> 00:59:54.886
Oh, boy! Grandma sent over another one
of her crummy herring pies again!

552
00:59:54.988 --> 00:59:58.754
Um, would you please sign
this receipt for me?

553
00:59:59.759 --> 01:00:01.659
I hate Grandma's stupid pies.

554
01:00:07.500 --> 01:00:10.060
She can't possibly have been
her granddaughter.

555
01:00:22.582 --> 01:00:25.517
Do you think we can still
make it in time?

556
01:00:49.642 --> 01:00:51.166
Look!
Tombo's down there!

557
01:00:51.277 --> 01:00:53.609
We can still make it.

558
01:00:59.252 --> 01:01:01.948
That certainly was
quite an ordeal.

559
01:01:02.055 --> 01:01:04.148
That boy waited
a very long time.

560
01:01:04.257 --> 01:01:07.693
Doesn't matter anyway.
I can't go in these wet clothes.

561
01:01:20.073 --> 01:01:21.540
Kiki, what's wrong?

562
01:01:21.641 --> 01:01:23.541
Do you have a headache?

563
01:01:24.644 --> 01:01:28.580
Why don't we grab a bite to eat?
I know I'm famished.

564
01:01:55.275 --> 01:01:57.209
Kiki!

565
01:02:18.298 --> 01:02:20.198
Not feeling very well, huh?

566
01:02:22.902 --> 01:02:26.804
- You have quite a fever.
- Is someone pounding on my head?

567
01:02:26.906 --> 01:02:29.932
I'll bet you never dried yourself off
completely yesterday.

568
01:02:31.044 --> 01:02:33.444
Am I gonna shrivel up and die?

569
01:02:36.916 --> 01:02:40.374
You have a cold, is all.
I'll bring up some medicine.

570
01:02:40.487 --> 01:02:42.955
And you should eat something.

571
01:02:43.056 --> 01:02:44.216
I'm not hungry.

572
01:02:44.324 --> 01:02:46.918
It'll be better if you eat now.

573
01:02:47.026 --> 01:02:50.052
How about some oatmeal with raisins?
Like some, Jiji?

574
01:02:55.602 --> 01:02:58.628
Oatmeal's the best thing
for a cold.

575
01:02:58.738 --> 01:03:00.729
There you go.

576
01:03:01.908 --> 01:03:04.172
Don't burn your tongue.

577
01:03:07.614 --> 01:03:11.448
Come and eat your oatmeal
before it gets cold.

578
01:03:11.551 --> 01:03:13.451
Do I have to eat?

579
01:03:13.553 --> 01:03:14.952
If you want to get well.

580
01:03:15.054 --> 01:03:18.455
That boy was in the shop
a while ago this morning.

581
01:03:18.558 --> 01:03:19.957
Huh?

582
01:03:20.059 --> 01:03:25.258
When I told him you were sick,
he asked how a witch could catch a cold.

583
01:03:26.199 --> 01:03:28.793
Oh, yes. He said he wanted
to visit you a little later.

584
01:03:28.902 --> 01:03:30.267
Oh, no!

585
01:03:31.437 --> 01:03:34.998
I figured you might say that,
so I politely refused.

586
01:03:35.108 --> 01:03:37.576
You're tired.
Just relax and sleep.

587
01:03:39.812 --> 01:03:42.542
I'll just open this window
so you have a little air.

588
01:03:48.788 --> 01:03:51.655
- Osono.
- Hmm?

589
01:03:51.758 --> 01:03:53.953
Um, never mind.

590
01:04:22.221 --> 01:04:23.415
Jiji!

591
01:04:24.657 --> 01:04:26.591
Jiji!

592
01:04:26.693 --> 01:04:28.126
What?

593
01:04:55.455 --> 01:04:57.821
Jiji!
Breakfast is ready!

594
01:04:57.924 --> 01:04:59.118
Kiki?

595
01:04:59.225 --> 01:05:02.854
- Feeling better this morning?
- Much better, thank you.

596
01:05:02.962 --> 01:05:05.192
I'm sorry.
I didn't realize I'd overslept.

597
01:05:05.298 --> 01:05:09.359
That's okay. Come down here.
I have a favor to ask of you.

598
01:05:09.469 --> 01:05:11.027
Okay.

599
01:05:11.137 --> 01:05:12.729
"Koppori."
Is that right?

600
01:05:12.839 --> 01:05:14.864
Uh-huh.
Is this enough money?

601
01:05:14.974 --> 01:05:17.875
That's all right.
It's close enough to walk from here.

602
01:05:17.977 --> 01:05:20.502
Don't be silly.
Work is work.

603
01:05:20.613 --> 01:05:22.740
And be sure to deliver it
to him direct.

604
01:05:25.418 --> 01:05:26.783
Jiji!

605
01:05:27.820 --> 01:05:30.721
- You have work?
- It's not far away.

606
01:05:30.823 --> 01:05:32.051
Who's your friend?

607
01:05:32.158 --> 01:05:35.059
Lily's her name.
I'll be down.

608
01:05:35.161 --> 01:05:39.063
Don't worry. I'll be back in a minute.
Pleasure to meet you.

609
01:06:15.635 --> 01:06:16.829
Ahh!

610
01:06:27.280 --> 01:06:28.679
Wonderful.

611
01:06:38.191 --> 01:06:41.183
Hey! Miss Witch!

612
01:06:43.996 --> 01:06:48.456
- Taking a walk?
- I'm looking for someone named Koppori.

613
01:06:49.602 --> 01:06:51.001
Hey, that's my name!

614
01:06:52.805 --> 01:06:55.740
Go around that way.
I'll be right with you.

615
01:07:00.079 --> 01:07:01.569
I'll bet Osono planned this.

616
01:07:07.420 --> 01:07:09.320
Gee, thanks a lot.

617
01:07:13.226 --> 01:07:16.593
I want to apologize
for making you wait the other night.

618
01:07:18.231 --> 01:07:20.096
I'm sorry you got wet.

619
01:07:20.199 --> 01:07:24.067
Want to come over to my place?
I have something to show you.

620
01:07:25.605 --> 01:07:27.163
Come on! Hurry!

621
01:07:30.843 --> 01:07:33.778
That party was to celebrate
the completion of this thing.

622
01:07:35.948 --> 01:07:38.940
This is the engine
of a man-propelled plane.

623
01:07:39.051 --> 01:07:41.178
Like it?

624
01:07:41.287 --> 01:07:45.223
We're assembling the wings and the frame
at somebody else's house.

625
01:07:45.324 --> 01:07:48.885
I'm planning on flying this thing
during my summer vacation.

626
01:07:53.966 --> 01:07:57.868
I got it! Let's go to the beach where
that dirigible made a forced landing!

627
01:07:58.671 --> 01:07:59.695
"Dirigible"?

628
01:07:59.806 --> 01:08:01.899
You didn't see it on TV?

629
01:08:02.008 --> 01:08:04.738
- I was sleeping.
- Then we have to go!

630
01:08:04.844 --> 01:08:07.642
- We're going with this?
- Why not?

631
01:08:07.747 --> 01:08:11.205
I have to practice anyway.
Gotta build up my legs.

632
01:08:11.317 --> 01:08:13.251
Okay. Ready?

633
01:08:19.525 --> 01:08:21.516
I've never ridden
a bicycle before.

634
01:08:21.627 --> 01:08:23.527
Oh, boy! Even better!

635
01:08:23.629 --> 01:08:27.497
Brace the bike with your foot
until I get her revved up. Let's go!

636
01:08:34.574 --> 01:08:36.041
Okay!

637
01:08:45.685 --> 01:08:47.778
- Should I get off?
- No!

638
01:09:14.747 --> 01:09:16.305
Go faster! Go!

639
01:09:16.415 --> 01:09:18.474
That's great!
Hang in there!

640
01:09:21.988 --> 01:09:25.549
Swing your body to the inside
when we go around the curve.

641
01:09:25.658 --> 01:09:27.956
Otherwise it won't turn
very well.

642
01:09:29.562 --> 01:09:31.553
Now!

643
01:09:34.734 --> 01:09:36.702
Great!
You're doing fine!

644
01:09:45.645 --> 01:09:48.079
Yahoo! Great!

645
01:09:57.924 --> 01:10:00.757
- The dirigible, right?
- Right.

646
01:10:09.568 --> 01:10:10.933
We're flying!

647
01:10:38.030 --> 01:10:39.930
Tombo, are you okay?

648
01:10:40.032 --> 01:10:42.830
- Yeah. Are you all right?
- I'm okay.

649
01:11:04.423 --> 01:11:06.288
Does my face look that funny?

650
01:11:08.094 --> 01:11:12.121
I'm sorry, but when we flew
over that cliff, I was so scared!

651
01:11:16.402 --> 01:11:17.892
I was scared too.

652
01:11:18.871 --> 01:11:20.805
I'll bet you used some magic.

653
01:11:20.906 --> 01:11:23.466
I'm not sure.
I was so frightened.

654
01:11:23.576 --> 01:11:25.874
Your poor bike.
It's a mess.

655
01:11:28.748 --> 01:11:30.648
Oh, no!
Am I in trouble!

656
01:11:30.750 --> 01:11:34.311
- Will you look after the bike for me?
- What went wrong?

657
01:11:34.420 --> 01:11:37.617
I pedaled too hard!
That's why it busted!

658
01:11:37.723 --> 01:11:39.156
Wait there!

659
01:12:00.446 --> 01:12:04.746
Sure would be terrific to go around
the world in a dirigible like that.

660
01:12:04.850 --> 01:12:08.115
How'd it make you feel,
the first time you ever went flying?

661
01:12:08.220 --> 01:12:10.848
I can't recall.
I was too young to remember.

662
01:12:10.956 --> 01:12:13.857
But my mom told me
I wasn't scared a bit.

663
01:12:13.959 --> 01:12:17.861
Gosh, I sure wish I was born
into a witch family.

664
01:12:17.963 --> 01:12:21.091
You can just fly away
on a broomstick, but me...

665
01:12:21.200 --> 01:12:23.498
That's all I can do.

666
01:12:25.137 --> 01:12:28.300
I don't find flying that much fun.
It's more of a job to me.

667
01:12:28.407 --> 01:12:32.309
It's not fun for you, but I'd think it
would be, putting your talents to work.

668
01:12:32.411 --> 01:12:34.743
I sort of feel
my confidence slipping.

669
01:12:34.847 --> 01:12:39.250
But I'm glad I came with you today.
I feel better sitting by the ocean.

670
01:12:39.351 --> 01:12:43.151
I could bring you here anytime you want
and train myself at the same time.

671
01:12:43.255 --> 01:12:46.418
- You're a very nice person.
- You just found out?

672
01:12:46.525 --> 01:12:48.652
I used to think
you were some sort of clown.

673
01:12:48.761 --> 01:12:50.661
My mom says the same thing.

674
01:12:50.763 --> 01:12:55.223
"You clown! Quit looking up to the sky
and get back to your books!"

675
01:12:59.939 --> 01:13:02.840
- Tombo!
- Huh?

676
01:13:04.877 --> 01:13:07.345
- Hey! Guess what!
- What?

677
01:13:07.446 --> 01:13:09.971
Something good!
Come here!

678
01:13:10.082 --> 01:13:11.982
I'll be right back.
Wait here.

679
01:13:15.855 --> 01:13:18.551
They said we could go
in the dirigible. Coming?

680
01:13:18.657 --> 01:13:20.386
They what?
Wow! Of course!

681
01:13:20.493 --> 01:13:22.393
Hey, who's your girlfriend?

682
01:13:22.495 --> 01:13:25.760
That's Kiki the Witch.
She even flies. Come on over, Kiki!

683
01:13:25.865 --> 01:13:29.494
They're gonna show us around
inside that dirigible!

684
01:13:29.602 --> 01:13:30.762
No, thanks.

685
01:13:30.870 --> 01:13:33.896
Ah, come on.
It'll be fun.

686
01:13:34.006 --> 01:13:36.907
Express Home Delivery.
I'm positive that's her.

687
01:13:37.009 --> 01:13:40.035
- You mean she's a working girl?
- My, how independent.

688
01:13:40.146 --> 01:13:42.671
Come on.
I'll introduce you to everybody.

689
01:13:42.781 --> 01:13:45.341
No, thanks.
See you later.

690
01:13:45.451 --> 01:13:46.475
What's the matter?

691
01:13:50.556 --> 01:13:52.683
What are you so mad about?

692
01:13:52.791 --> 01:13:54.486
I'm not mad at all.

693
01:13:54.593 --> 01:13:57.994
I have a lot of work to do,
so just leave me alone.

694
01:14:02.134 --> 01:14:04.125
Tombo, forget her!
Come on!

695
01:15:41.468 --> 01:15:44.198
I think something's wrong with me.

696
01:15:44.305 --> 01:15:47.968
I make friends, then suddenly
I can't bear to be with any of them.

697
01:15:48.075 --> 01:15:50.669
Seems like that other me,
the cheerful and honest one...

698
01:15:50.778 --> 01:15:52.712
went away somewhere.

699
01:16:01.188 --> 01:16:03.088
Some friend you are.

700
01:16:34.205 --> 01:16:36.799
Jiji, I don't care
if you do have a girlfriend.

701
01:16:36.907 --> 01:16:39.239
You can't be late
for every meal.

702
01:16:39.343 --> 01:16:41.243
And clean up after yourself.

703
01:16:42.646 --> 01:16:45.012
What are you talking
like a cat for?

704
01:16:53.057 --> 01:16:54.024
Jiji.

705
01:16:54.125 --> 01:16:56.559
Oh, no! Talk to me!

706
01:16:56.660 --> 01:16:58.560
You mean
you can't speak anymore?

707
01:17:02.033 --> 01:17:03.523
Jiji!

708
01:17:03.634 --> 01:17:05.602
I wonder what happened to him.

709
01:17:05.703 --> 01:17:09.070
I can't figure out
a word he says anymore.

710
01:17:09.173 --> 01:17:10.435
Oh, my gosh!

711
01:17:34.498 --> 01:17:36.363
I'm losing my witch's powers.

712
01:18:35.659 --> 01:18:39.322
You can't fly anymore?
Have you lost your magic?

713
01:18:39.430 --> 01:18:44.458
It's become very weak, so I think I've
gotta take a break from delivery work.

714
01:18:44.568 --> 01:18:48.800
But I'll work really hard in the bakery,
so please let me stay in my room.

715
01:18:49.773 --> 01:18:51.172
Of course you can stay.

716
01:18:51.275 --> 01:18:54.176
Will your powers come back
after you've rested?

717
01:18:54.278 --> 01:18:57.577
I don't know. Maybe.
I can make another broom, but...

718
01:19:02.386 --> 01:19:03.978
Hey, look!

719
01:19:38.889 --> 01:19:43.519
It's me, Tombo. Did you see me today?
I was waving at you from the dirigible.

720
01:19:43.627 --> 01:19:46.596
The captain allowed me into the
control cabin during the test flight.

721
01:19:46.697 --> 01:19:48.130
It was great!

722
01:19:48.232 --> 01:19:50.723
<i>Hello?
Kiki, are you there?</i>

723
01:19:50.834 --> 01:19:52.802
Please don't call me anymore.

724
01:19:52.903 --> 01:19:57.363
<i>What? I can barely hear you.
The captain said he'd like to meet you.</i>

725
01:19:57.474 --> 01:19:59.840
What? Hey, come on!
Don't hang up!

726
01:20:03.380 --> 01:20:05.712
What's wrong?
You don't look like you feel well.

727
01:20:06.917 --> 01:20:09.010
I'm still training
to be a witch.

728
01:20:09.119 --> 01:20:13.385
If I lose my magic, that means
I've lost absolutely everything.

729
01:20:41.652 --> 01:20:42.619
Kiki!

730
01:20:44.455 --> 01:20:45.820
Hi!

731
01:20:48.392 --> 01:20:51.987
You didn't come pay me a visit,
so I had to come visit you.

732
01:20:52.096 --> 01:20:55.759
- I'm sorry.
- Well, I also came to shop a little.

733
01:20:55.866 --> 01:20:59.029
Come on in. I'm done now.
We can take a break.

734
01:20:59.136 --> 01:21:01.627
You'd better believe I will.

735
01:21:04.842 --> 01:21:07.743
- Nice place you have.
- Help yourself to these.

736
01:21:07.845 --> 01:21:11.008
- I'll make some fresh tea.
- No tea, thanks. Do you have some milk?

737
01:21:11.115 --> 01:21:12.514
Sure.

738
01:21:18.656 --> 01:21:19.918
Well, well.
Positively amazing.

739
01:21:20.024 --> 01:21:24.085
He's the spitting image of
that stuffed cat. You're Jiji, right?

740
01:21:26.830 --> 01:21:28.957
How's the home delivery business?

741
01:21:33.070 --> 01:21:36.767
- That bad, huh?
- I'm not working much now.

742
01:21:46.417 --> 01:21:49.181
I thought
you seemed depressed.

743
01:21:49.286 --> 01:21:51.948
I didn't know things like that
happened to witches.

744
01:21:57.594 --> 01:22:00.495
Hey! Why not come and
stay at my little place?

745
01:22:00.597 --> 01:22:02.326
Huh?

746
01:22:02.433 --> 01:22:06.096
Tell your boss you need a break.
They can live without you for a night.

747
01:22:06.203 --> 01:22:07.830
How about it, pussy cat?

748
01:22:12.976 --> 01:22:14.876
Rather be
with your girlfriend, huh?

749
01:22:14.978 --> 01:22:16.639
Come on! Let's go!

750
01:22:27.458 --> 01:22:29.551
Hurry!
The bus is leaving!

751
01:23:19.877 --> 01:23:22.072
I'm bushed!

752
01:23:23.480 --> 01:23:25.311
It's so beautiful here.

753
01:23:34.391 --> 01:23:38.828
Must've been blind, with two
beautiful girls in front of him.

754
01:24:01.251 --> 01:24:04.186
What do you mean,
you thought I was a boy?

755
01:24:04.288 --> 01:24:06.722
Well, look at the way
you're dressed.

756
01:24:06.824 --> 01:24:09.987
Tell me what kind of boy
has these legs, mister.

757
01:24:18.101 --> 01:24:21.002
- Crows!
- We've become real close friends.

758
01:24:21.104 --> 01:24:22.469
Wow.

759
01:24:22.573 --> 01:24:25.371
Hello, everybody.
We're home again.

760
01:24:25.476 --> 01:24:28.206
Good afternoon.
I'm sorry I bothered you before.

761
01:24:33.584 --> 01:24:37.145
Make yourself at home
while I get some water.

762
01:25:31.975 --> 01:25:33.374
Like it?

763
01:25:33.477 --> 01:25:34.671
Amazing.

764
01:25:34.778 --> 01:25:37.747
I got the idea for it
after we met the first time.

765
01:25:38.682 --> 01:25:42.311
But I really haven't got
the girl's face right.

766
01:25:42.419 --> 01:25:45.445
I've been waiting for you to come back
to get it right.

767
01:25:45.556 --> 01:25:47.854
- You mean, that's me?
- Yes.

768
01:25:47.958 --> 01:25:50.324
Would you be my model?

769
01:25:50.427 --> 01:25:52.486
But I'm not very beautiful.
Why do you want me?

770
01:25:57.301 --> 01:26:01.567
You've got a great face. Besides,
it's prettier than it was the last time.

771
01:26:01.672 --> 01:26:04.698
Come on. Don't be scared.
Sit here.

772
01:26:08.178 --> 01:26:10.305
Lift up your head a little.

773
01:26:10.414 --> 01:26:13.577
Look beyond the horizon.
Don't move. Very good.

774
01:26:15.018 --> 01:26:17.919
Painting and magical powers
seem to be very similar.

775
01:26:18.021 --> 01:26:22.253
- Sometimes I can't paint a thing.
- You mean it? Then what happens?

776
01:26:22.359 --> 01:26:24.987
Kiki, don't move!
Don't look over here.

777
01:26:27.397 --> 01:26:30.958
Without even thinking about it
I used to be able to fly.

778
01:26:31.068 --> 01:26:34.595
Now I can't even begin to remember
how I ever managed to do it.

779
01:26:37.007 --> 01:26:39.976
At times like that,
you know what I do? Paint.

780
01:26:40.077 --> 01:26:42.011
That gets rid of my frustrations.

781
01:26:42.112 --> 01:26:46.481
- But still, if I can't fly...
- Then I just stop.

782
01:26:46.583 --> 01:26:49.017
Take long walks,
look at the scenery, doze off at noon.

783
01:26:49.119 --> 01:26:51.053
Don't do a single thing.

784
01:26:51.154 --> 01:26:53.554
Then, suddenly,
you'll be able to fly again.

785
01:26:53.657 --> 01:26:55.056
Maybe that'll help.

786
01:26:55.158 --> 01:26:58.286
Trust me. It'll happen.
Come on, don't ruin the pose.

787
01:27:19.316 --> 01:27:23.912
When I was your age,
I'd already decided to become an artist.

788
01:27:24.021 --> 01:27:27.457
I loved painting.
I even painted in my sleep.

789
01:27:27.557 --> 01:27:30.754
Then one day, for no reason,
I became unable to paint.

790
01:27:31.995 --> 01:27:35.260
So I painted and painted some more,
but none of it was any good.

791
01:27:35.365 --> 01:27:39.825
They were copies of paintings
I'd seen somewhere before.

792
01:27:39.936 --> 01:27:42.928
Just copies of ones
I'd seen somewhere.

793
01:27:43.040 --> 01:27:45.270
I swore I'd paint my own pictures.

794
01:27:46.376 --> 01:27:47.604
That must've been hard.

795
01:27:49.312 --> 01:27:52.713
But after that...
it's not much easier now.

796
01:27:52.816 --> 01:27:56.582
I think I found what painting means,
at least for me.

797
01:27:58.655 --> 01:28:01.317
To fly, you don't chant
a spell or something, right?

798
01:28:01.425 --> 01:28:04.258
Mm-hmm.
We fly with our spirit.

799
01:28:04.361 --> 01:28:07.728
The witch's spirit? Perfect!
That's what I'm talking about.

800
01:28:07.831 --> 01:28:10.823
The spirit of witches.
The spirit of artists.

801
01:28:10.934 --> 01:28:12.561
The spirit of bakers!

802
01:28:13.370 --> 01:28:16.464
I suppose it must be
a power given by God.

803
01:28:16.573 --> 01:28:18.564
Sometimes you suffer for it.

804
01:28:19.876 --> 01:28:23.334
I guess I never gave witchcraft
much thought.

805
01:28:23.447 --> 01:28:27.315
That talk about discipline and training
was so old-fashioned.

806
01:28:27.417 --> 01:28:30.352
I was so happy that you came
all that way to see me.

807
01:28:30.454 --> 01:28:35.221
If I had been alone tonight, I would've
been one giant ball of frustration.

808
01:28:35.325 --> 01:28:40.661
There have been many times I've thought
of painting over that painting.

809
01:28:40.764 --> 01:28:43.130
Why?
It's so beautiful.

810
01:28:43.233 --> 01:28:44.598
You know,
when I saw you today...

811
01:28:44.701 --> 01:28:47.602
I looked at your sad face
and thought, "I've found it!"

812
01:28:47.704 --> 01:28:51.105
- I knew I could paint you.
- But that's not fair!

813
01:28:53.176 --> 01:28:55.906
All's fair in love and art.

814
01:28:56.012 --> 01:28:57.946
- Let's go to sleep.
- Okay.

815
01:29:00.517 --> 01:29:04.214
- Sorry about taking your bed from you.
- Don't worry about it.

816
01:29:06.823 --> 01:29:08.552
Can I visit you
once in a while?

817
01:29:08.658 --> 01:29:12.958
Sure. Anytime during the summer.
That is, if I can visit you too.

818
01:29:13.063 --> 01:29:14.462
Uh-huh!

819
01:29:18.602 --> 01:29:19.602
<i>The intercontinental dirigible
Freedom Adventurer...</i>

820
01:29:21.238 --> 01:29:23.103
<i>recently downed
in a spectacular forced landing...</i>

821
01:29:23.206 --> 01:29:26.664
<i>due to torrential rains
just outside the city limits...</i>

822
01:29:26.777 --> 01:29:28.802
<i>has now been repaired.</i>

823
01:29:28.912 --> 01:29:31.107
Hello.
Gutiokipan Bakery.

824
01:29:31.214 --> 01:29:33.148
Kiki, how was it?

825
01:29:34.584 --> 01:29:37.951
Take plenty of time
and get rested up.

826
01:29:38.054 --> 01:29:41.854
<i>That elderly lady you made the delivery
for has something else for you to take.</i>

827
01:29:41.958 --> 01:29:43.448
<i>Should I tell her no?</i>

828
01:29:43.560 --> 01:29:47.257
I've told her you'd be away
for some time, but she kept insisting.

829
01:29:48.131 --> 01:29:51.225
Then stop on your way back.
Bye.

830
01:30:10.554 --> 01:30:12.988
- Afternoon, ma'am.
- Well, well.

831
01:30:13.089 --> 01:30:15.956
We've been expecting you.
Come in.

832
01:30:17.894 --> 01:30:21.625
<i>There are less than five minutes
to takeoff now.</i>

833
01:30:23.400 --> 01:30:26.733
- Very nice to see you again, ma'am.
- I'm glad you came.

834
01:30:26.837 --> 01:30:31.399
Excuse me for not standing, but my legs
are bothering me more than usual.

835
01:30:31.508 --> 01:30:32.873
Bertha, bring the package.

836
01:30:32.976 --> 01:30:34.443
Yes!

837
01:30:34.544 --> 01:30:36.512
I hope it hasn't taken off yet.

838
01:30:36.613 --> 01:30:37.773
Not yet.

839
01:30:37.881 --> 01:30:41.373
Bertha's absolutely mad
about lighter-than-air travel.

840
01:30:41.484 --> 01:30:43.384
I'm the adventuresome type.

841
01:30:44.554 --> 01:30:46.522
Turn the volume down.

842
01:30:47.357 --> 01:30:49.882
Would you open the box?

843
01:30:49.993 --> 01:30:51.426
Uh-huh.

844
01:30:58.501 --> 01:31:00.162
You want me to deliver it?

845
01:31:00.270 --> 01:31:03.171
Would you please deliver it
to a girl named Kiki?

846
01:31:03.273 --> 01:31:05.468
She was kind to me
and a tremendous help.

847
01:31:05.575 --> 01:31:07.475
It's my way of saying "thank you."

848
01:31:07.577 --> 01:31:11.479
And would you find out
when her next birthday might be?

849
01:31:11.581 --> 01:31:14.482
Then I'll be able
to bake her another one.

850
01:31:19.723 --> 01:31:21.122
Kiki.

851
01:31:24.527 --> 01:31:28.520
I will. And I'm sure Kiki will
want to know the lady's birthday...

852
01:31:28.632 --> 01:31:31.100
so she'll be able
to give her a present.

853
01:31:31.201 --> 01:31:33.135
You've got a deal.

854
01:31:47.050 --> 01:31:50.110
- What happened?
- There's been a terrible catastrophe.

855
01:31:50.220 --> 01:31:52.984
<i>Oh, no! The tie-down ropes holding
the blimp are breaking one by one!</i>

856
01:31:53.089 --> 01:31:55.421
<i>It's drifting straight toward
our television cameras.</i>

857
01:31:55.525 --> 01:31:58.358
<i>My God, it's going to...</i>

858
01:32:00.163 --> 01:32:03.826
Oh! They always leave me hanging
at the most exciting part!

859
01:32:04.668 --> 01:32:07.136
These winds always come
in midsummer.

860
01:32:07.237 --> 01:32:09.432
They'll be hitting us
pretty soon.

861
01:32:13.243 --> 01:32:15.370
It'll pass by quickly.
Don't worry.

862
01:32:15.478 --> 01:32:17.412
Oh, goody, it's back on.
Look!

863
01:32:20.784 --> 01:32:23.309
Look at that!
It's completely upside-down!

864
01:32:23.420 --> 01:32:27.322
<i>The Freedom Adventurer
has been shaken by great winds...</i>

865
01:32:27.424 --> 01:32:29.415
It's like a balloon
in that position.

866
01:32:29.526 --> 01:32:33.394
<i>It has broken loose from its mooring and
drifted into an upside-down position.</i>

867
01:32:33.496 --> 01:32:37.398
<i>A desperate, last-ditch effort is
being made to tie the dirigible down...</i>

868
01:32:37.500 --> 01:32:39.434
<i>and keep it from drifting away.</i>

869
01:32:40.470 --> 01:32:45.840
<i>It's extremely doubtful whether
it can be done... Oh, no! It's useless!</i>

870
01:32:45.942 --> 01:32:49.434
That's my friend Tombo
holding on to that rope!

871
01:32:49.546 --> 01:32:52.947
<i>... attached to the end of the cable
as though it were a toy!</i>

872
01:32:53.049 --> 01:32:56.018
<i>There's a young boy
hanging on to the cable!</i>

873
01:32:56.119 --> 01:32:59.316
<i>He's being lifted away
along with the police car!</i>

874
01:32:59.422 --> 01:33:02.619
<i>I don't believe what I'm seeing!
Oh, the humanity!</i>

875
01:33:02.726 --> 01:33:06.093
- Are you sure it's your friend?
- I have to go!

876
01:33:06.196 --> 01:33:08.858
- Be careful!
- Oh, dear. What's happening?

877
01:33:32.989 --> 01:33:36.254
Hold on there, son!
Just hold your grip steady!

878
01:33:36.359 --> 01:33:38.224
Release the helium
from the tail!

879
01:34:03.486 --> 01:34:08.549
<i>All citizens are requested
to remain calm. Do not panic.</i>

880
01:34:08.658 --> 01:34:11.559
<i>The helium inside the dirigible
will not explode.</i>

881
01:34:12.362 --> 01:34:13.852
Tombo.

882
01:34:14.564 --> 01:34:17.089
Any word about the boy
hanging on the rope?

883
01:34:17.200 --> 01:34:20.601
The latest report was that
the police car dropped into a pool!

884
01:34:34.384 --> 01:34:36.443
<i>Clear the street!
Get on the sidewalk!</i>

885
01:34:36.553 --> 01:34:38.680
<i>You there in that car!
Do not block the street!</i>

886
01:34:43.393 --> 01:34:45.122
Are you feeling all right?

887
01:34:50.300 --> 01:34:52.700
Please, sir,
may I borrow your broom?

888
01:34:52.802 --> 01:34:55.532
- Huh?
- I promise I'll bring it right back.

889
01:34:55.638 --> 01:34:58.539
- Well, I suppose that's okay.
- Thank you very much!

890
01:35:35.512 --> 01:35:36.809
Fly.

891
01:35:39.516 --> 01:35:40.915
Oh, my goodness!

892
01:35:52.695 --> 01:35:54.959
Hey! Oh, no!

893
01:35:59.702 --> 01:36:01.101
Look out!

894
01:36:08.711 --> 01:36:11.179
Straighten up and fly right,
or I'll burn you!

895
01:36:18.555 --> 01:36:19.988
The boy appears safe...

896
01:36:20.089 --> 01:36:23.354
but the dirigible is on a collision
course directly for the clock tower.

897
01:36:23.459 --> 01:36:25.723
If the wind doesn't shift direction...

898
01:36:25.828 --> 01:36:28.695
<i>the Freedom Adventurer
will surely smash into the tower!</i>

899
01:36:30.066 --> 01:36:33.058
We gotta get up higher!
We're gonna hit the tower!

900
01:36:33.169 --> 01:36:34.830
There's not enough helium!

901
01:36:34.938 --> 01:36:37.338
Before we hit,
jump onto the tower!

902
01:36:37.440 --> 01:36:38.839
Aye, aye, Captain!

903
01:36:38.942 --> 01:36:41.342
Hey there!
Over here! Come on!

904
01:36:41.444 --> 01:36:44.470
- Get out of the way!
- Grab hold of this!

905
01:37:01.531 --> 01:37:03.658
That way! Hurry!

906
01:37:03.766 --> 01:37:05.233
Oh, no!

907
01:37:19.515 --> 01:37:21.881
That sound
is the helium gas leaking.

908
01:37:21.985 --> 01:37:25.443
The condition of the boy is unknown.
From where I'm standing... Oh, no!

909
01:37:30.493 --> 01:37:33.394
Too much gas has escaped,
and it's falling!

910
01:37:43.906 --> 01:37:45.840
It's snagged
on another building!

911
01:37:45.942 --> 01:37:48.911
- Hey, look! Over there!
- It's a miracle!

912
01:37:49.012 --> 01:37:51.708
The boy has managed
to keep hold of the rope!

913
01:37:51.814 --> 01:37:54.715
It's a miracle!
But how can anyone rescue him now?

914
01:37:54.817 --> 01:37:57.547
That boy is hanging on
for dear life.

915
01:37:57.654 --> 01:37:59.554
Something just flew by!

916
01:37:59.656 --> 01:38:01.055
Is it a bird?

917
01:38:01.157 --> 01:38:04.320
No, no, it's not a bird!
It's a young girl!

918
01:38:04.427 --> 01:38:07.328
<i>Yes, there is a young girl
soaring through the sky!</i>

919
01:38:07.430 --> 01:38:09.330
Wow! Go, girl!

920
01:38:09.432 --> 01:38:12.094
- She can fly now!
- Get 'em, Kiki!

921
01:38:12.201 --> 01:38:13.463
Tombo!

922
01:38:14.570 --> 01:38:15.764
Kiki!

923
01:38:18.174 --> 01:38:21.837
Come on!
Be a good broom and help me out!

924
01:38:21.944 --> 01:38:24.071
Hang on, young fella!
Don't give up!

925
01:38:24.180 --> 01:38:26.944
Hold on!
She's almost there!

926
01:38:27.050 --> 01:38:29.518
Tombo!

927
01:38:29.619 --> 01:38:30.745
Kiki!

928
01:38:36.626 --> 01:38:38.526
Hold on!
Don't give up now!

929
01:38:40.897 --> 01:38:42.489
Don't give up, son.

930
01:38:46.602 --> 01:38:49.503
Don't give up! Don't give up!

931
01:38:57.313 --> 01:39:01.215
She caught him in midair!
I've never seen anything so amazing!

932
01:39:24.073 --> 01:39:26.974
That broom is mine.
I gave it to her myself.

933
01:39:27.076 --> 01:39:29.601
She did it!
She did it!

934
01:39:30.680 --> 01:39:32.614
You're so brave, Kiki.

935
01:39:32.715 --> 01:39:34.342
Positively amazing.

936
01:39:36.586 --> 01:39:38.486
Better call the hospital.

937
01:39:38.588 --> 01:39:40.488
I'll be ready any minute now.

938
01:39:48.398 --> 01:39:49.797
Jiji!

939
01:42:30.953 --> 01:42:33.217
We just got a letter
from Kiki!

940
01:42:36.926 --> 01:42:41.659
"Dear Mother and Father,
How are you doing? Jiji and I are fine."

941
01:42:41.764 --> 01:42:44.733
<i>Regarding my work, it certainly seems
everything is falling into place.</i>

942
01:42:44.834 --> 01:42:46.768
<i>I'm even starting
to gain some confidence.</i>

943
01:42:46.869 --> 01:42:49.030
<i>There are still times
when I feel sad...</i>

944
01:42:49.138 --> 01:42:51.265
<i>but all in all,
I sure love this town.</i>
